== 2. The two facts the round rests on, in the code on main (Source) ==
- A move by /clear or /background keeps the binding's generation: carry builds the new
  binding as a copy of the old (cmd/handoff/session.go, "nu := b"), so Gen is unchanged.
- handoff role gives a new generation each time it is run, in the same session too:
  bind writes Gen: now.UnixNano() (cmd/handoff/session.go).
The second is why I note that role spare, run again by the spare itself after away, would
stop it being the spare the away entry names.
